---
description: >-
  HOTEL and ROOM declare attribute types containing an unescaped comma
  inside parentheses (GEOMETRY(point,4326), DECIMAL(10,2)) and attribute
  names containing an unescaped period (room.number, bed.type) without
  backtick-escaping, checking the parser tolerates these special
  characters directly - contrast with the sibling "backtick-escaped"
  fixture, which requires escaping the same kind of characters.
config:
  loglevel: 1
---
erDiagram
  HOTEL {
  string               address
  GEOMETRY(point,4326) location
  DECIMAL(10,2)        price_per_night
  }
  HOTEL ||--o{ ROOM : has
  ROOM {
  int room.number
  string bed.type
  }
